.TH DANBY-MAYPREDATOR 1
.SH NAME
danby-maypredator \- May predator-prey limit-cycle model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/maypredator
.SH MODEL
X' = rX(1-X/K)-aXY/(X+A);
Y' = sY(1-Y/(bX)).
.PP
Prey have logistic growth and saturating predation.  Predator carrying
capacity is proportional to available prey.  The interaction can destabilize
the positive equilibrium and produce an attracting limit cycle.
.SH DISPLAY
The phase portrait distinguishes convergence to an equilibrium from repeated
motion around a limit cycle.  The adjacent histories reveal amplitude and
predator lag.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set initial populations.  The six tracks set prey
growth and capacity, attack and half-saturation, predator growth, and prey
support.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The implementation handles the prey-free boundary explicitly, avoiding the
singularity in Y/(bX).  Its positive analytic equilibrium and boundary
derivative are checked by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/maypredator.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/maypredator.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-logisticprey (1),
.IR numerics (2)
